By exercising a permission in this license, you agree to its conditions. The permissions below are granted by AnslmC only to the extent AnslmC has authority to grant them.

## 2. Public Access

Anyone may access, view, and download publicly available source code for the Covered Software. You may clone or make a source-only fork of the public repository, including through GitHub, subject to the source-publication conditions in Section 4. These permissions do not by themselves authorize commercial use or distribution of an Installable or Executable Version.

## 3. Personal and Private Use

You may make and use modifications privately for Personal Use, including learning, experimentation, and local testing. Personal Use may include privately testing a modification that could technically be used in a Competing Product. You do not need permission merely because a private modification has competing functionality, provided that you comply with the restrictions on publication, commercial use, and executable distribution in this license.

Personal Use does not authorize making a Competing Product available to others, publishing source to establish or promote a Competing Product, using Covered Software commercially, or distributing an Installable or Executable Version.

## 4. Permitted Source-Code Publication

You may publish or otherwise distribute Source Code, including modified Source Code and source-only repository forks, only for a noncommercial purpose that is not intended to establish, offer, market, or promote a Competing Product. This permission applies only to Source Code and is subject to Section 7.

Publishing Source Code as the code for, or as a means to establish or promote, a Competing Product is not permitted without the Rights Holder's prior written authorization, even if the publication itself is free. A permitted source publication does not grant its recipients permission to use the Covered Software commercially or to distribute an Installable or Executable Version.

Sharing Source Code is distinct from distributing a built, bundled, compiled, or otherwise installable or executable version. A public repository or source-only fork is not an Installable or Executable Version merely because a recipient could independently build or package it.

### Commentary, Documentation, and Technical Discussion

Notwithstanding Sections 4 and 6, you may create, reproduce, publish, and distribute tutorials, reviews, articles, documentation, explanations, and technical discussions about AnswerSense for commercial or noncommercial purposes. This permission includes reproducing limited excerpts of unmodified Source Code only to the extent reasonably necessary for explanation, criticism, review, or discussion. The excerpts, individually and in the aggregate, must not reproduce substantial portions of the Source Code or provide it as a substitute for accessing the Covered Software.

This permission is limited to those publications and necessary excerpts. It does not authorize publishing modified Source Code, establishing, offering, marketing, or promoting a Competing Product, distributing an Installable or Executable Version under Section 5, or any other Commercial Use under Section 6. Those activities remain subject to the restrictions and authorization requirements elsewhere in this license.

## 5. Installable or Executable Distribution

You may not distribute, publish, offer, transmit, or otherwise make an Installable or Executable Version of the Covered Software, or a derivative extension based on it, available to another person without the Rights Holder's prior written authorization. This restriction applies whether distribution is free or paid and includes, without limitation, the Chrome Web Store, other extension stores, GitHub Releases, direct downloads, and equivalent channels.

This restriction does not prohibit you from running Covered Software locally for Personal Use under Section 3. This license does not claim to prevent anyone from technically building or packaging publicly available source code; it grants no permission to distribute the resulting Installable or Executable Version without authorization.

